---
import { CONTEXT } from "../config";
import SectionHeader from "./SectionHeader.astro";

/**
 * What a connect costs, and the one setting that changes it.
 *
 * This section exists because the saving is the largest number on the whole
 * site and it was reachable only from the CHANGELOG. Nothing here is Bastion's
 * argument for itself in the abstract — every figure is measured by the app's
 * own _Test_ step, from the listing as it arrived on the wire, and the profile
 * that carries them is named so a reader can check it against their own.
 *
 * It sits after `HowItWorks` and before `Audit`: the runtime section has just
 * finished saying that a client points at a URL and gets one child, and this is
 * the next thing that happens on that connection. Put after `Audit` it would
 * separate the record from the window that shows it.
 *
 * The honest half is not an afterthought paragraph, it is the reason the switch
 * ships off: a saving whose cost is only in the CHANGELOG is a saving somebody
 * turns on and then discovers.
 */

/**
 * The small bar, as a share of the large one.
 *
 * Derived rather than typed, and typed nowhere: `0.4k` against `26.2k` is about
 * 1.5%, which is a sliver — that IS the picture, and a bar rounded up to
 * something comfortable would be drawing a different claim than the figure
 * beside it. Both strings carry the same `k`, so the units cancel and
 * `parseFloat` is enough; `max()` keeps the sliver from disappearing entirely
 * on a narrow column.
 */
const share = (parseFloat(CONTEXT.facadeTokens) / parseFloat(CONTEXT.tokens)) * 100;
---

<section class="wrap py-[96px]">
  <div class="flex flex-wrap items-start gap-16">
    {/* The count is read from the constant, not typed into the heading: it is
        the same figure the bar beside it carries, and a heading is the last
        place anybody thinks to update. Past thirty it is a digit — `SPELLED`
        stops there on purpose. */}
    <SectionHeader
      eyebrow="The context cost"
      heading={`${CONTEXT.tools} tool definitions, on every connect.`}
    >
      <p class="m-0 text-[16px] leading-[1.6] text-fg-dim text-pretty">
        Every client wired to a profile is sent every tool definition that profile's server exposes
        before it can call one, and holds them for the whole conversation. That is the largest fixed
        charge a shared gateway imposes: <code class="font-mono text-[14.5px]">{CONTEXT.profile}</code
        > is {CONTEXT.tools} tools and about {CONTEXT.tokens} tokens, in every editor that opens it, every
        time one starts.
      </p>
      <p class="m-0 text-[15px] leading-[1.6] text-fg/55 text-pretty">
        <strong class="font-semibold text-fg/80">Load tools on demand</strong> serves {
          CONTEXT.facadeTools
        } tools in their place — a search, a describe and a call — and the same profile connects at
        about {CONTEXT.facadeTokens}. The full searchable index costs {CONTEXT.indexTokens}, and only
        if something asks for it. Nothing becomes unreachable, and Bastion measures both numbers itself:
        the profile row carries the figure rather than leaving it to be inferred.
      </p>

      {/* The trade, in the same accent-rule treatment `HowItWorks` gives the
          thing it admits to giving up. It is not a caveat in small print for
          the same reason it is off by default. */}
      <p class="m-0 border-l-2 border-accent pl-4 text-[14.5px] leading-[1.6] text-fg/70 text-pretty">
        What it costs is on the client's side, and the switch says so: every call reaches the editor
        as <code class="font-mono text-[13.5px]">bastion_call_tool</code>, so one approval rule there
        now covers every tool on that server. Bastion's own write gate is unaffected — a write tool
        is still absent from the index and still refused by the dispatcher. The editor's gate is the
        coarser one, which is why this ships off and why a profile can disagree with the app-wide
        answer.
      </p>
      <p class="m-0 text-[13px] leading-[1.6] text-fg/45 text-pretty">
        MCP has no method for fetching a schema later — <code class="font-mono text-[12px]"
          >inputSchema</code
        > is required in a <code class="font-mono text-[12px]">tools/list</code> entry — so an index and
        a dispatcher is the only shape lazy discovery can take. Doing it in the gateway is what keeps
        it honest: the call is opened back up into the ordinary <code class="font-mono text-[12px]"
          >tools/call</code
        > it stands for before the audit chain, the Activity window or the write gate sees the frame,
        so all three go on naming the real tool. A facade bought as a server cannot do that.
      </p>
    </SectionHeader>

    <div class="flex min-w-[min(420px,100%)] flex-1 basis-[520px] flex-col gap-4">
      <div class="reveal flex flex-col gap-6 rounded-lg border border-white/9 bg-white/3 p-8">
        {/* The profile is NOT inside the eyebrow: `.eyebrow` uppercases, and a
            server id typed back in caps is an id nobody can match against their
            own config. */}
        <div class="flex flex-wrap items-baseline justify-between gap-3">
          <h3 class="eyebrow m-0 text-fg-muted">On connect</h3>
          <span class="font-mono text-[12px] text-fg-dim">{CONTEXT.profile}</span>
        </div>

        <div class="flex flex-col gap-5">
          <div class="flex flex-col gap-2.5">
            <div class="flex flex-wrap items-baseline justify-between gap-2">
              <span class="text-[13.5px] font-medium">Every tool, as any gateway serves it</span>
              <span class="font-mono text-[12px] text-danger-ink">
                {CONTEXT.tools} tools · ~{CONTEXT.tokens}
              </span>
            </div>
            <div class="h-2.5 w-full rounded-full bg-danger/45"></div>
          </div>

          <div class="flex flex-col gap-2.5">
            <div class="flex flex-wrap items-baseline justify-between gap-2">
              <span class="text-[13.5px] font-medium">Tools on demand</span>
              <span class="font-mono text-[12px] text-ok-ink">
                {CONTEXT.facadeTools} tools · ~{CONTEXT.facadeTokens}
              </span>
            </div>
            <div class="h-2.5 w-full rounded-full bg-white/6">
              <div
                class="h-2.5 rounded-full bg-ok"
                style={`width:max(${share.toFixed(1)}%,5px)`}
              >
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="flex items-baseline gap-3.5 border-t border-white/8 pt-5">
          <span
            class="font-display text-[44px] leading-none font-semibold tracking-[-0.03em] text-accent"
          >
            {CONTEXT.cut}
          </span>
          <span class="text-[13.5px] leading-[1.5] text-fg-dim text-pretty">
            fewer tokens to hand a client the same server. The index it can ask for costs {
              CONTEXT.indexTokens
            }.
          </span>
        </div>

        <p class="m-0 font-mono text-[11px] leading-[1.6] text-fg/38 text-pretty">
          Counted from the listing as it arrived on the wire, at four bytes to the token, with the
          profile's write gate already applied.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="flex flex-col gap-4 rounded-lg border border-white/9 bg-white/[2.5%] p-8">
        <h3 class="eyebrow m-0 text-fg-muted">What the client is served instead</h3>
        <dl class="m-0 flex flex-col">
          {
            CONTEXT.facade.map((t) => (
              <div class="flex flex-wrap items-baseline gap-x-5 gap-y-1 border-b border-rule py-3.5 last:border-b-0 last:pb-0">
                <dt class="basis-[172px] shrink-0 font-mono text-[12.5px] text-accent-hi">
                  {t.name}
                </dt>
                <dd class="m-0 flex-1 basis-[220px] text-[13.5px] leading-[1.55] text-fg-dim text-pretty">
                  {t.v}
                </dd>
              </div>
            ))
          }
        </dl>
        <p class="m-0 text-[13px] leading-[1.6] text-fg/45 text-pretty">
          One switch in Settings moves every profile at once; a profile that disagrees — one wired to
          a client that already defers tool schemas by itself, and so gains nothing here — overrides
          it in its own sheet.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
